# `x.mod(0)` is division by zero — must PANIC on BOTH backends. LLVM-Mod
# emitted a bare `srem`/`urem` with no div0 guard (`urem x,0` / `srem x,0`
# is UB, garbage on aarch64). NON-CONSTANT 0 divisor so the check reaches
# the backend Mod arm rather than being constant-folded.
void main():
    int x = 7
    int zero = 0
    int r = x.mod(zero)
    print(f"{r}")
